index.html

<html>
<head>
<title>Types of CSS</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="mystyle.css">
<style>
body{background-color:wheat}
h3{color:green;font-style:italic}
</style>
</head>
<body style="text-align:center">
<h2 style="color:red">Welcome to Java Web Programming CSS using INLINE CSS</h2>
<p style="color:blue;font-size:25px;font-style:italic">CSS styles webpages in three ways.</p>
<h3>Internal CSS Style</h3>
<ul>
<li>Inline CSS: Styles one element using the style attribute.</li>
<li>Internal CSS: Styles one page using the style tag.</li>
<li>External CSS: Styles pages using a separate CSS file.</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>


